#!/usr/bin/python3 -I
"""govee-wow v4 - a club / 4DX-style light show for World of Warcraft: Forever (LAN only).

  govee-wow                 status
  govee-wow demo [secs] [style]   the whole show on the real lights, then restore (75 s)
  govee-wow when couch      only in couch mode (TV plugged in)  [default]
  govee-wow when always     whenever WoW / Battle.net runs
  govee-wow when never      off
  govee-wow palette NAME    auto (by zone) | club | velvet | midnight | neon
  govee-wow level N         master brightness 10-100 (default 100), on top of the style caps
  govee-wow max [STYLE N]   per-style brightness cap in % (what the lights may reach at most):
                            daylight 60, party 55, standard 50, comfort 45, afterdark 2 (1-10)
  govee-wow style NAME      comfort | standard | party | afterdark | daylight
  (schedule in config.json: 23-7 afterdark, 7-18 daylight, 19-20 party, else standard)
  daylight = greens matched to the game's terrain: ceiling = sky/canopy, lamps = ground
             rising into foliage, wind + sun dapples, sun arc teal morning -> gold evening
  govee-wow afterdark auto  switch to afterdark automatically at night (23:00-07:00); off
  govee-wow afterdark level N   after-dark brightness 1-10 % (default 2)
  govee-wow preview [s] [style]   emulator: draws the show in this terminal, lights untouched
  govee-wow watch           live mirror of what the real lights are doing right now
  govee-wow check           flash/photosensitivity analysis of every style (WCAG 2.3.1)
  govee-wow daemon          background service (systemd: govee-wow.service)

The room is one canvas: lamp - ceiling ring - lamp. Everything is choreographed on it.
  Programs (the base look, follow the game):
    explore  "drone swarm": glowing points glide through the room over a flowing palette
    lounge   resting in a city / inn: slow, deep, warm
    cruise   mounted: light streaks race up the lamps, a comet circles the ceiling
    combat   128 BPM: kick pulses, the lamps are VU meters of your action, ceiling chase
    boss     140 BPM: purple/blue lighthouse sweeps, white-pink hits on the downbeat
    dead     blackout to deep blue, a slow flatline pulse
    + low health: a red heartbeat that speeds up as you drop
  Cues (one-shot effects, ~0.1 s after they happen in game):
    each spell you cast  -> a pink shockwave falls from the ceiling down the lamps
    big cooldown         -> riser fills the lamps bottom to top, then bursts
    kill                 -> firework: a rocket climbs the lamp and bursts into sparkles
    hit taken            -> red surge from the floor;  big heal -> blue shimmer rising
    new target           -> ceiling blip;  pulling into combat -> red "drop" wipe
    level up / boss kill -> 5 s finale;  quest / achievement -> gold shimmer
    zone change          -> palette wipe across the room
Real-time data comes from the CouchLights addon (an 8-pixel strip in the top-left corner,
read from the screen). Without it the combat log file is used (1-3 s late).
Screen capture uses GNOME's own screencast API on the TV (no "share your screen" dialog),
starts once the WoW window has been up a few seconds, runs at capture_fps (15), and falls back
to the desktop portal (one dialog, then a saved token) if that API is unavailable.
Flash safety: every style stays within WCAG 2.3.1 (<= 3 flashes/s); "comfort" also caps how
fast any light may change brightness, so it cannot strobe at all.
Tuning: ~/.config/govee-wow/config.json.
"""
